## Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)

### How long is the 2026 PGA TOUR season?
January 15 - September 27, 2026

### Which signature events award 700 FedExCup points?
The eight limited-field Signature Events listed above each award 700 points to the winner.

### How do I watch PGA TOUR?
Via PGA TOUR LIVE on ESPN+, Paramount+ (CBS), Golf Channel/NBC Sports, or the official PGA TOUR app.

### What is the FedExCup?
The season-long points race culminating in the FedExCup Playoffs and Tour Championship—awarding bonus pools and tour titles.

### Has the TOUR Championship format changed for 2026?
No. All 30 qualifiers now begin at even par for a standard 72-hole stroke-play event.

### What is the cut rule at regular PGA TOUR events?
Full-field tournaments cut to the low 65 professionals and ties after 36 holes.

### What happens if a tournament ends in a tie?
A sudden-death playoff begins on a hole chosen by the tournament committee and continues hole-by-hole until one player wins a hole outright.

### Where can I buy tickets or hospitality passes?
Visit the individual tournaments page on PGATOUR.com and follow the tickets link. (https://www.pgatour.com/tickets)

### Are fans allowed to bring cameras?
Cameras are permitted only during practice rounds. During competition rounds, phones are allowed but must be silenced, and flash photography is prohibited.

### What is the dress code for spectators?
There’s no formal dress code, but golf-appropriate attire is encouraged. Comfortable shoes are highly recommended for walking the course.

### How do weather delays affect play?
If weather suspends play, the round resumes as soon as conditions allow. Completion may be delayed to the next day, but tournaments aim to finish on Sunday whenever possible.

